{"id":"3f54b531-cd5a-4857-8618-183da91a4612","revision":0,"last_node_id":27,"last_link_id":21,"nodes":[{"id":7,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1110,270],"size":[280,160],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Models in this Workflow","properties":{},"widgets_values":["### z_image_turbo_int8_convrot:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main)\n\n### qwen_3_4b_int8_convrot:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main)\n\n### ae-turbo:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/vae)"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"### z_image_turbo_int8_convrot:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main)\n\n### qwen_3_4b_int8_convrot:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Z-Image-Base-Turbo-INT8-Convrot/tree/main)\n\n### ae-turbo:\n[Link to the file](https://huggingface.co/Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo/tree/main/vae)"},"color":"#2a363b","bgcolor":"#3f5159"},{"id":8,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1110,490],"size":[280,310],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Note","properties":{},"widgets_values":["### Important\nThe Style & Prompt Encoder (\"Positive\") node already contains advanced built-in prompt presets. If you choose to use one of these presets, it might change some aspects of the chosen Wildcard, keep that in mind.\n\n### ImpactWildcardProcessor\nWildcard is a reusable text placeholder that randomly inserts one entry from a predefined list, adding variety and reducing prompt repetition.\n\nTo use a Wildcard, create a .txt file inside the wildcards folder of the Impact Pack (custom_nodes/ComfyUI-Impact-Pack/wildcards). Each line in the file represents a different prompt entry.\n\nLeave the Wildcard field empty and write the prompt normally if you don't want to use Wildcards.\n\nI’ve created an upgrade for this node that allows for the dynamic use of keywords within prompts. If you’re interested, check out the link below:\n[Link to the page](https://github.com/VictorDmAlves/comfyui-keyword-wildcard-processor)\n\n### Tips\n\nTo generate different Wildcard combinations, keep Batch Size = 1 and increase the Batch Count/Queue Count instead. Each new execution re-rolls the Wildcards, while Batch Size usually reuses the same resolved prompt for every image in the batch.\n\n### Resolution\n* Portrait (896x1152)\n* Square (1024x1024)\n* Landscape (1216x832)"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"### Important\nThe Style & Prompt Encoder (\"Positive\") node already contains advanced built-in prompt presets. If you choose to use one of these presets, it might change some aspects of the chosen Wildcard, keep that in mind.\n\n### ImpactWildcardProcessor\nWildcard is a reusable text placeholder that randomly inserts one entry from a predefined list, adding variety and reducing prompt repetition.\n\nTo use a Wildcard, create a .txt file inside the wildcards folder of the Impact Pack (custom_nodes/ComfyUI-Impact-Pack/wildcards). Each line in the file represents a different prompt entry.\n\nLeave the Wildcard field empty and write the prompt normally if you don't want to use Wildcards.\n\nI’ve created an upgrade for this node that allows for the dynamic use of keywords within prompts. If you’re interested, check out the link below:\n[Link to the page](https://github.com/VictorDmAlves/comfyui-keyword-wildcard-processor)\n\n### Tips\n\nTo generate different Wildcard combinations, keep Batch Size = 1 and increase the Batch Count/Queue Count instead. Each new execution re-rolls the Wildcards, while Batch Size usually reuses the same resolved prompt for every image in the batch.\n\n### Resolution\n* Portrait (896x1152)\n* Square (1024x1024)\n* Landscape (1216x832)"},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":9,"type":"SDXLEmptyLatentSizePicker+","pos":[1110,860],"size":[280,230],"flags":{"pinned":tr